  'nc-network-engineering-level-4', 'Network Engineering — Level 4', 'ict', 4, 'Advanced', 'Network Engineering Level 4 is an intermediate–advanced qualification designed to equip learners with the knowledge and practical skills to design, install, configure, secure, and troubleshoot modern computer networks. The course builds on foundational IT and networking skills and prepares learners for industry roles as junior network engineers, support technicians, and infrastructure specialists.', 'Prior industry experience and completion of the relevant lower-level competencies are recommended; no formal platform prerequisite is enforced.', 'UNVERIFIED', 'CHCN L4', 49, 1160, 'published', 1)
